{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.40.100","page_type":"section"},"citation":"18.40.100","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.40.100","content_hash":"47386954b0eba77d160b57e8be0ae259b36fb55318123523b6aea7b646fa33a2","heading":"Pavement alignment.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.100:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.40.100","text":"Horizontal and vertical alignment of pavement on all streets, except in unusual cases, shall be as follows:\n(a) Horizontal Alignment. Minimum radii at the centerline of right-of-way:\n(1) Major traffic thoroughfares:\n(i) Primary: 500 feet.\n(ii) Secondary: 300 feet.\n(2) Collectors: 200 feet.\n(3) Minor streets: 100 feet.\nA tangent shall be provided between all reverse curves of sufficient length as related to the radius so as to provide for a smooth flow of vehicular traffic.\n(b) Vertical Alignment. All changes in the pavement grade shall be connected by a vertical curve of such length as to provide for a sufficient sight distance and shall be subject to the approval of the City or County Engineer, whichever shall apply. (Code 1981 § 41-98. Code 1995 § 134-140.)\nCross References: City Engineer, TMC 2.20.100 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"d841323e-4091-5ed6-83b4-fb4d5eb310c4"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.40.100","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.40.100","content_hash":"ab35d71518599e4a1d12b2c0d7e36303eeae1ed9c3ae07a3a7c6737e0647a3a3","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.100:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.40.100:block:0",